       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient would be at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other toxicity. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify a dose that high.\n\nWas this a typo? Usual adult doses are:\n- **Depression, OCD, or PTSD:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, with a usual range of 50\u2013200 mg.\n- **Panic disorder or social anxiety:** start at 25 mg once daily, with a usual range of 50\u2013200 mg.\n\nIf you meant a different dose, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away, for example sertraline 100 mg PO once daily. If you really do want 600 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy before it's released."
